Dear Alexander,

pimplot() and truthTable() belong to different packages, so getting an error message for one function and not the other can happen.

The message reads such that there is no column highpatent in the results object that could be fed into the plotting function. I remember I once had the same problem, but, unfortunately, I don't remember whether and how I could fix it. You may check the column names in solT$tt$recoded.data to see whether highpatent is included. It could be an upper-case/lower-case issue, but I don't think so because this should happen to everyone.

I am sorry I don't have a quick fix to offer.

Kind regards

Ingo

